Chapter: J1939

 SAE J1939, the CAN-bus higher-layer protocol for heavy-duty vehicles,
 agricultural equipment (ISOBUS), and industrial machinery. A message
 is carried in a 29-bit extended CAN identifier that packs a priority
 (bits 26-28), the extended data page and data page (25, 24), the PDU
 format (16-23), the PDU specific (8-15), and the source address
 (0-7), plus up to eight data bytes. The Parameter Group Number (PGN)
 names the message: for PDU2 format (PDU format 240 or above) it
 includes the PDU-specific group extension; for PDU1 (below 240) the
 PDU-specific field is a destination address and is not part of the PGN.

Section: Identifier Construction

  j1939-can-id : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  j1939-can-id (priority) (pf) (ps) (source-addr) =
   bit-or (bit-or (bit-shl priority 26) (bit-shl pf 16)) (bit-or (bit-shl ps 8) source-addr)

Section: PGN

  j1939-pgn-pdu2 : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  j1939-pgn-pdu2 (pf) (ps) = bit-or (bit-shl pf 8) ps

  j1939-pgn-pdu1 : Integer -> Integer
  j1939-pgn-pdu1 (pf) = bit-shl pf 8

  j1939-is-pdu1 : Integer -> Boolean
  j1939-is-pdu1 (pf) = pf < 240

Section: Identifier Fields

  j1939-priority : Integer -> Integer
  j1939-priority (can-id) = bit-and (bit-shru can-id 26) 7

  j1939-pf : Integer -> Integer
  j1939-pf (can-id) = bit-and (bit-shru can-id 16) 255

  j1939-ps : Integer -> Integer
  j1939-ps (can-id) = bit-and (bit-shru can-id 8) 255

  j1939-source-addr : Integer -> Integer
  j1939-source-addr (can-id) = bit-and can-id 255

  j1939-pgn : Integer -> Integer
  j1939-pgn (can-id) =
   let pf = j1939-pf can-id
   in if j1939-is-pdu1 pf then j1939-pgn-pdu1 pf else j1939-pgn-pdu2 pf (j1939-ps can-id)

Section: Common Parameter Groups

  j1939-pgn-request : Integer = #EA00
  j1939-pgn-tp-cm : Integer = #EC00
  j1939-pgn-tp-dt : Integer = #EB00
  j1939-pgn-address-claim : Integer = #EE00
  j1939-pgn-engine-hours : Integer = #FEE5
  j1939-pgn-engine-temp : Integer = #FEEE

  j1939-addr-global : Integer = #FF
  j1939-addr-null : Integer = #FE
